nt","header_size":"h3"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"60e4db3","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"Jones r\u00e8gne sur la cat\u00e9gorie des mi-lourds pendant plus d\u2019une d\u00e9cennie. Il bat des noms prestigieux comme Lyoto Machida, Vitor Belfort, Alexander Gustafsson ou encore son rival Daniel Cormier."},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"6e7c4af","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"Apr\u00e8s une pause de trois ans, il revient en 2023 dans une nouvelle cat\u00e9gorie : les poids lourds. Face \u00e0 Ciryl Gane, il d\u00e9montre que le temps et le changement de division n\u2019ont pas entam\u00e9 sa supr\u00e9matie. En quelques minutes, il soumet le Fran\u00e7ais et s\u2019adjuge une nouvelle ceinture."},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"4cf8b70","elType":"widget","settings":{"image_size":"full","_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"16","right":"0","bottom":"32","left":"0","isLinked":false},"image":{"url":"https:\/\/www.ufc.fr\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/04\/portrait-ufc-jon-jones-domination.webp","id":3229,"size":"","alt":"","source":"library"}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"image"}],"isInner":true},{"id":"cda78e5","elType":"container","settings":{"content_width":"full","flex_gap":{"column":"16","row":"16","isLinked":true,"unit":"px","size":16},"hover_parallax":[{"layer_position_vr":{"unit":"%","size":30},"layer_position_hr":{"unit":"%","size":40},"_id":"9e73a49"},{"layer_position_vr":{"unit":"%","size":60},"layer_position_hr":{"unit":"%","size":20},"_id":"e0f1aae"}]},"elements":[{"id":"cd0db46","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"Un style unique et impr\u00e9visible","header_size":"h3"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"7d944af","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"John Jones est l\u2019incarnation de la polyvalence. Excellent en lutte, impr\u00e9visible en striking, dot\u00e9 d\u2019un mental d\u2019acier, il s\u2019adapte \u00e0 chaque adversaire avec une ma\u00eetrise quasi chirurgicale. Que ce soit au sol, en clinch ou en distance, il trouve toujours la faille."},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true},{"id":"43c55bd","elType":"container","settings":{"content_width":"full","flex_gap":{"column":"16","row":"16","isLinked":true,"unit":"px","size":16},"hover_parallax":[{"layer_position_vr":{"unit":"%","size":30},"layer_position_hr":{"unit":"%","size":40},"_id":"9e73a49"},{"layer_position_vr":{"unit":"%","size":60},"layer_position_hr":{"unit":"%","size":20},"_id":"e0f1aae"}]},"elements":[{"id":"b13a8af","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"Le GOAT du MMA ?","header_size":"h3"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"10b617c","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"Si sa carri\u00e8re a \u00e9t\u00e9 ponctu\u00e9e de controverses, son palmar\u00e8s et sa long\u00e9vit\u00e9 parlent d\u2019eux-m\u00eames. John Jones est consid\u00e9r\u00e9 par beaucoup comme le Greatest of All Time (GOAT) du MMA. Peu de combattants peuvent se targuer d\u2019avoir domin\u00e9 deux divisions majeures, sur deux \u00e9poques diff\u00e9rentes."},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true},{"id":"e87e6f8","elType":"container","settings":{"content_width":"full","width":{"unit":"%","size":30,"sizes":[]},"width_tablet":{"unit":"%","size":100,"sizes":[]},"width_mobile":{"unit":"%","size":"","sizes":[]},"flex_gap":{"column":"48","row":"48","isLinked":true,"unit":"px","size":48},"html_tag":"aside","hover_parallax":[{"layer_position_vr":{"unit":"%","size":30},"layer_position_hr":{"unit":"%","size":40},"_id":"af953d2"},{"layer_position_vr":{"unit":"%","size":60},"layer_position_hr":{"unit":"%","size":20},"_id":"09731c5"}]},"elements":[{"id":"3be26dd","elType":"container","settings":{"content_width":"full","flex_gap":{"column":"24","row":"24","isLinked":true,"unit":"px","size":24},"hover_parallax":[{"layer_position_vr":{"unit":"%","size":30},"layer_position_hr":{"unit":"%","size":40},"_id":"eedba79"},{"layer_position_vr":{"unit":"%","si